{
  "mcpServers": {
    "gmail": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@gongrzhe/server-gmail-autoauth-mcp"]
    }
  },
  "_notes": [
    "Structure only: copy the 'gmail' entry into your MCP client's config (for Claude Code: claude mcp add gmail -- npx -y @gongrzhe/server-gmail-autoauth-mcp). This file holds no secrets.",
    "The server reads its Google OAuth client from ~/.gmail-mcp/gcp-oauth.keys.json (YOUR Google Cloud OAuth client file; create it in the Google Cloud console, never commit it).",
    "After the one-time browser sign-in the server stores its token in ~/.gmail-mcp/credentials.json (never commit it). See the server's README for the sign-in step.",
    "The pipeline's live sender (notify.McpSender) launches this same command itself over stdio, so it does not need this file. It only needs the two ~/.gmail-mcp files above.",
    "Live mode (python main.py --send-live) also needs NOTIFY_TO set to the address that should receive the notices, e.g. export NOTIFY_TO=you@example.com"
  ]
}
